        "also_known_as": [],
        "biography": "Lawrence D. Lieber (/\u02c8li\u02d0b\u0259r/; born October 26, 1931) is an American comic book writer and artist best known as the co-creator of the Marvel Comics superheroes Iron Man, Thor, and Ant-Man. He is also known for his long stint both writing and drawing the Marvel Western Rawhide Kid and for illustrating the newspaper comic strip The\u00a0Amazing Spider-Man from 1986 to 2018. From 1974 to 1975, he was editor of Atlas/Seaboard Comics. Lieber is the younger brother of Stan Lee, who had been a writer, editor, and publisher of Marvel Comics.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Larry Lieber, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.",
